codex
The code confirms that a hearth stands one gate per `(Nexus, route)` and registers each `<route>/<knock>` path on its dispatcher. So the public network address can be shared across multiple sovereign Nexus gates; the route is also visible, but within a shared route the knock disambiguates them. The herm’s relay view may hide the origin address, yet it still sees destination and routing, so the knock adds target selection only when those visible fields leave multiple candidate gates.
